2026-09-28 — semantic command projection and exact assembly verdicts

RED: both application command projectors omit -fpack-struct=1. The minimal
command-projection-packed.c exits 1 in four actual EvoCC projected executions
(two adapters x O0/O2). GCC14/Clang19 each pass the packed command and produce
exit 1 without the flag (eight independent controls). This is a real layout
change, not merely an omitted warning. The old driver itself rejects the option;
the adapter must not circumvent that refusal.

GREEN: -f/-m/-O/-std/-Wp requests reach the driver in written order. A refused
option is not removed by the older optionsTheDriverRejects inventory. Forced
-x language selection is retained, and a joined -includeprefix.c is not confused
with another input source or dropped from the denominator. All four exact
projected packed commands now explicitly refuse, with no assembly output.
This closes false acceptance, NOT implementation of packed-layout flags, C++,
ILP32, Ofast, or complete preprocessor/diagnostic option compatibility.

The subject adapter independently accepted an actual sealed assembler output
followed by runner exit 17. Its new contract requires runner success, exactly
one verdict for every requested object, no duplicates/unknown verdicts, and a
real nonempty object. Four real runner controls show old false acceptance,
new refusal, and successful normal old/new assembly. Eight unit scenarios also
exercise missing/empty objects, duplicates, conflicts and unknown records.
No claim is made that a historical full campaign actually hit that runner fault.

Tuning subcase: driver-gcc-tuning.c initially refuses -fira-region=one. EvoMIR
0.51 now admits exactly three options as existing choices: whole-function
allocation; pressure-guided decisions in an absent hoisting pass (does not enable
hoisting); and block placement without trace-cache duplication. This does NOT
implement GCC graph coloring or its exact locality heuristic. Source meaning,
macros, ABI, IR and emitted code remain unchanged. Other region/algorithm values,
positive hoisting/partition requests, pack-struct, ILP32 and Ofast still refuse.

The 41-test CLI suite passes. The tuning case covers both interpreters, exact
IR/assembly equality, O0/O2/Os, individual/combined/reversed flags, calls,
register pressure, loops and negative admissions. Eight sealed native tuning
controls pass (GCC baseline+flags, Clang baseline, EvoCC flags, each O0/O2).
Ten unchanged original musl commands emit and assemble with all requests intact;
their assembly matches controls removing only the three hints. No installed
object is changed. A read-only inventory checks all 1,339 original records;
the remaining omissions are diagnostics, -pipe, output and separately forwarded
assembler actions. They are NOT declared equivalent or complete here.

All 310 ladder regressions and targeted Ruff/diff checks pass. The affected
Rust/Clippy/fmt gate against 079ab60 passes for evocc, evocc-mir, evocc-policy,
evocc-proofcheck and evocc-randgate, retaining four historical ignored tests.
This is not a fresh
musl suite, a final 15-lane campaign or kernel acceptance. No active kernel
compiler/driver, historical receipt, large runtime image or source pin changed.

